#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0107 expect=skipped domain=EX
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when the EC domain is present and Treatment Vehicle Amount Units (EXVAMTU) is present in the EX dataset.
#note "AUTHORED BY Plan B phase 4c (grounding R-B2: this rule had NO scenario directory at all, so its whole EC dependency shipped unpinned). EX carries EXVAMTU, and there is NO EC block. The rule declares Requirements.Datasets [EC], so the run cannot answer it and RuleRunner skips at the Requirements gate — BEFORE AbsentDatasetSkip.decide. Until 4c the same shape was an authored ds_exists(\"EC\") conjunct that evaluated FALSE and reported nothing: an EXECUTED-and-silent verdict indistinguishable from a rule that looked and found nothing. Sister of CDISC-CG0105-skipped_no_ec_dataset-EX."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset EX class=INTERVENTIONS label="Exposure"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col EXSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col EXTRT   type=Char label="Name of Treatment"
col EXVAMTU type=Char label="Planned Amount Units"
---
S1 | EX | 001 | 1 | DRUGA | mL
S1 | EX | 001 | 2 | DRUGA | mL
---
